# oracle: the scalar orientation components of fix colvars (colvarcomp_rotations.cpp): orientationAngle,
#   orientationProj, tilt (axis 1 1 0, normalized), spinAngle (axis z, periodic), eulerPhi, eulerPsi and eulerTheta of 6
#   atoms against reference positions rotated by 0.6 rad, shifted and perturbed, each under a harmonic restraint. The
#   optimal rotation of the centred reference onto the group's positions minus their centre of geometry, and the
#   gradients through the leading eigenvector's derivative (colvar_rotation_derivative.h prepare_derivative,
#   project_force_to_C_from_dxdq, project_force_to_group2).
# Measured with native LAMMPS: state files byte-identical; the traj equal to every printed digit to step 25, then
#   within 4.3e-13 (the restraint forces amplify the LJ trajectory's last-bit differences).
# oracle-inputs: w777cv_orient.colvars
# oracle-files: or.colvars.traj or.colvars.state
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 filerel=1e-10
units           lj
atom_modify     map array
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
set             atom 1*128 type 2
mass            1 1.0
mass            2 2.5
velocity        all create 1.5 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all colvars w777cv_orient.colvars output or
fix_modify      2 energy yes
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[2][1] f_2[3][1] f_2[4][1] f_2[5][1] f_2[6][1] f_2[7][1]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             50
run             30
